WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.893
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:16.163 --> 00:19.416
[theme music playing]

3
00:26.632 --> 00:28.175
[liquid bubbling]

4
00:32.763 --> 00:35.516
[clinking, rattling]

5
00:35.599 --> 00:36.684
[cat meows]

6
00:37.643 --> 00:39.478
[hoofbeats]

7
00:41.397 --> 00:42.273
[water splashes]

8
00:49.154 --> 00:50.990
[handcuffs rattling, click]

9
00:51.532 --> 00:53.450
LOVE IN DISGUISE

10
00:56.662 --> 00:57.830
Yesterday…

11
00:59.206 --> 01:01.667
I realized that I may have assumed…

12
01:02.293 --> 01:04.962
Uh, sorry, what was that about yesterday, sir?

13
01:06.171 --> 01:08.299
It seems I misinterpreted your intentions,

14
01:08.382 --> 01:10.467
but anyone in my position would have.

15
01:11.302 --> 01:12.261
Right, I see.

16
01:12.344 --> 01:13.554
Okay, I'll just go.

17
01:13.637 --> 01:14.805
-Do it here. -[gasps]

18
01:15.764 --> 01:17.099
-[gasps] -For the first time in a while,

19
01:17.182 --> 01:18.517
I've made up my mind.

20
01:19.310 --> 01:21.854
Anyway… here's what I'm getting at.

21
01:21.937 --> 01:23.147
[Jae-hee] Can you please stop moving?

22
01:23.230 --> 01:24.064
I'm just… Wait.

23
01:24.148 --> 01:25.524
-Ugh, I heard you! -Where do you think you're going?

24
01:25.608 --> 01:26.942
-I'm talking to you! -I said I get it!

25
01:27.026 --> 01:28.819
[grunts, exclaims]

26
01:28.903 --> 01:30.487
-[gasps] -[Yi-jun grunts]

27
01:31.697 --> 01:33.115
[strained grunts]

28
01:34.617 --> 01:37.286
[upbeat passionate music playing]

29
01:59.058 --> 02:01.685
KUNMANDU

30
02:02.269 --> 02:03.646
[Jae-hee's dad sighs, clears throat]

31
02:04.188 --> 02:06.315
Hold on a sec. I should give the princess a call.

32
02:06.398 --> 02:07.232
[Jae-hee's mom groans]

33
02:07.316 --> 02:10.194
Why are you calling her so early when she's too busy to even come home?

34
02:10.611 --> 02:11.654
You're right.

35
02:11.737 --> 02:13.197
[groans] You'll annoy her. Just leave it.

36
02:13.280 --> 02:14.406
[inhales]

37
02:14.490 --> 02:17.743
It's just… I had the most peculiar dream last night, that's all.

38
02:17.826 --> 02:18.827
What about?

39
02:19.328 --> 02:20.162
Well, you see,

40
02:20.245 --> 02:21.622
I dreamt of a white steed.

41
02:21.705 --> 02:23.540
I could tell it had an amazing pedigree.

42
02:24.375 --> 02:26.585
It was galloping right towards me.

43
02:27.878 --> 02:30.381
-[rhythmic chopping] -[horse neighing]

44
02:30.464 --> 02:33.050
[romantic orchestral music playing]

45
02:33.759 --> 02:36.679
[Jae-hee's dad] Then, a dashing knight…

46
02:36.762 --> 02:37.638
[neighs]

47
02:37.721 --> 02:40.057
…elegantly dismounted from the horse

48
02:41.392 --> 02:44.645
and majestically dipped the other person with one arm.

49
02:44.728 --> 02:46.814
Then, Jae-hee…

50
02:46.897 --> 02:48.440
Oh, my goodness. [gasps]

51
02:48.524 --> 02:50.442
Oh my, this must be a sign.

52
02:50.526 --> 02:52.903
You see, the knight dipped Jae-hee.

53
02:52.987 --> 02:54.113
It means she's dating a guy!

54
02:54.697 --> 02:56.907
Or… getting married! Even better!

55
02:56.991 --> 02:58.575
[laughing]

56
02:59.743 --> 03:01.078
She was the one riding.

57
03:01.161 --> 03:03.163
-[comical music playing] -Riding what?

58
03:03.247 --> 03:04.248
The white steed.

59
03:04.790 --> 03:07.501
The knight on the white steed was our daughter.

60
03:08.252 --> 03:10.587
Oh, jeez, were you even listening to the story?

61
03:10.671 --> 03:12.715
[Jae-hee's mom] Oh, for goodness sake. Ugh.

62
03:12.798 --> 03:13.924
[intense drum beating]

63
03:14.883 --> 03:17.344
[gentle romantic music playing]

64
03:17.428 --> 03:18.512
Who's the princess then?

65
03:19.013 --> 03:20.097
That's the thing.

66
03:20.639 --> 03:21.473
There was…

67
03:21.974 --> 03:24.393
this pale-looking normal guy…

68
03:25.102 --> 03:27.062
that… needed rescuing.

69
03:28.897 --> 03:31.316
[dreamy romantic music playing]

70
03:37.531 --> 03:39.366
[Jae-hee's mom] What a pointless dream.

71
03:39.450 --> 03:40.659
Whatever it takes,

72
03:40.743 --> 03:42.870
I'll get Jae-hee to marry that punk on the white steed.

73
03:43.454 --> 03:45.748
Daughters tend to follow their mother's footsteps.

74
03:46.915 --> 03:47.791
Don't say that.

75
03:47.875 --> 03:49.752
You take that back!

76
03:49.835 --> 03:50.669
[spits]

77
03:50.753 --> 03:51.628
Watch what you say!

78
03:52.421 --> 03:54.423
Ugh, I'm telling you, if Jae-hee ever brings home

79
03:54.506 --> 03:56.008
some pale-looking punk, I'll…

80
03:56.091 --> 03:56.967
I'll smack him.

81
03:57.051 --> 03:58.719
I'll smack him with a bunch of green onions.

82
03:58.802 --> 03:59.887
I swear I'll do it.

83
04:02.056 --> 04:03.682
What are you looking at?

84
04:04.308 --> 04:07.269
Um, upon visual inspection, you seem fine.

85
04:07.352 --> 04:08.187
Are you okay?

86
04:08.270 --> 04:09.480
What if I said I wasn't?

87
04:09.897 --> 04:11.023
-Would you keep this up? -[gasps]

88
04:11.106 --> 04:12.024
-[groans] -Oops.

89
04:12.107 --> 04:14.568
[grunts, groans]

90
04:17.654 --> 04:18.489
[exhales]

91
04:21.950 --> 04:24.078
You slammed me again.

92
04:24.870 --> 04:25.746
Again!

93
04:26.789 --> 04:29.875
Allow me to continue where you left off earlier, sir.

94
04:29.958 --> 04:33.670
What you were about to say to me was that I ap…

95
04:34.254 --> 04:35.255
Apply yourself.

96
04:36.673 --> 04:37.508
Apply myself?

97
04:37.591 --> 04:39.802
Apply yourself and do the job right.

98
04:39.885 --> 04:41.929
Wait, what do you mean you want me to do the job right?

99
04:42.012 --> 04:43.806
What? Should I do it?

100
04:44.306 --> 04:45.474
Wow.

101
04:46.475 --> 04:47.434
Whatever.

102
04:48.602 --> 04:49.436
I'm going out.

103
04:49.520 --> 04:50.521
[sighs]

104
04:51.021 --> 04:52.231
[chiming effect]

105
04:52.940 --> 04:54.274
Oh, you want me to come along?

106
04:54.358 --> 04:56.652
I see you've already forgotten what your job is.

107
04:56.735 --> 04:57.736
I have not.

108
04:57.820 --> 04:59.071
I'm your personal secretary,

109
04:59.154 --> 05:01.115
but yesterday, you told me to stay put.

110
05:01.198 --> 05:04.201
You told me to wait in the car and stay away from the second floor.

111
05:05.828 --> 05:07.788
You really do hold a grudge, don't you?

112
05:08.247 --> 05:10.582
I also said I'm 50/50 on you.

113
05:11.291 --> 05:13.335
Half trust, half skeptical.

114
05:14.920 --> 05:17.381
If you want to earn my trust, put your back into it.

115
05:18.882 --> 05:20.509
[Jae-hee] Wait till I find the proof.

116
05:21.093 --> 05:22.886
I'll bust your tight abs.

117
05:23.512 --> 05:24.805
Why are you still here?

118
05:25.430 --> 05:27.432
I'll catch a cold if I stand around.

119
05:29.184 --> 05:30.144
[inhales]

120
05:34.439 --> 05:35.607
[quiet frustrated scream]

121
05:36.233 --> 05:37.067
[grunts]

122
05:37.776 --> 05:39.820
Oh, I wish I could beat him up, just for me.

123
05:40.654 --> 05:41.530
[sighs]

124
05:49.413 --> 05:52.124
[tense music playing]

125
06:03.969 --> 06:06.221
EPISODE 3

126
06:07.264 --> 06:10.100
[light music playing]

127
06:27.367 --> 06:28.702
[exhales]

128
06:29.286 --> 06:30.162
[inhales]

129
06:30.245 --> 06:31.496
[groaning]

130
06:32.414 --> 06:33.373
[exhales]

131
06:34.333 --> 06:35.626
[Hye-jung] If you wanna pretend we're strangers,

132
06:35.709 --> 06:36.835
we should commit to that.

133
06:37.211 --> 06:39.546
But if you wanna dance, let's hit the floor.

134
06:41.840 --> 06:43.884
[soft music playing]

135
07:13.580 --> 07:14.456
[glass clinking]

136
07:14.957 --> 07:16.375
[liquid sloshing]

137
07:17.376 --> 07:18.335
[glass clinks]

138
07:25.759 --> 07:28.762
[machine whirring]

139
07:29.596 --> 07:31.014
[soft chuckle] You're awake.

140
07:31.598 --> 07:32.432
Good morning.

141
07:32.516 --> 07:34.601
[sucks teeth, exhales]

142
07:34.685 --> 07:35.894
Did you sleep well?

143
07:37.062 --> 07:40.107
Oh, the Taekang Goddess has returned.

144
07:40.190 --> 07:41.400
I had fun last night.

145
07:41.858 --> 07:42.776
You had fun?

146
07:43.360 --> 07:44.278
[inhales]

147
07:44.361 --> 07:46.029
Have I already become a thing of the past?

148
07:47.281 --> 07:48.573
Was last night a letdown?

149
07:49.491 --> 07:50.534
It wasn't for me.

150
07:51.159 --> 07:51.994
[soft chuckle]

151
07:53.245 --> 07:54.079
Same for me.

152
07:54.579 --> 07:55.414
Oh, yeah?

153
07:55.497 --> 07:58.458
I'll say yes to some guys, have a good time, and send them home.

154
07:59.543 --> 08:00.711
That's how I feel.

155
08:00.794 --> 08:02.838
[wistful music playing]

156
08:07.843 --> 08:09.011
[Hye-jung] I'll get going.

157
08:12.222 --> 08:13.724
-[door lock beeps] -[door opens]

158
08:14.766 --> 08:15.851
-[door closes] -[door lock beeps]

159
08:15.934 --> 08:17.352
Is that line trending?

160
08:22.274 --> 08:23.108
[groans]

161
08:23.191 --> 08:25.110
[grunting]

162
08:26.778 --> 08:27.696
[soft grunt]

163
08:30.240 --> 08:32.993
[humming]

164
08:35.787 --> 08:36.621
[soft chuckle]

165
08:36.705 --> 08:39.166
You're fascinating, Lee Hye-jung.

166
08:44.713 --> 08:45.839
Wow.

167
08:52.262 --> 08:54.306
[Jae-hee] Whoa, how many watches does he need?

168
08:54.389 --> 08:56.892
[quirky upbeat music playing]

169
08:56.975 --> 08:58.393
That's tacky.

170
08:59.019 --> 09:01.396
How can someone wear something like this?

171
09:04.024 --> 09:05.025
[sighs]

172
09:07.402 --> 09:09.363
[Jae-hee] Upon visual inspection, you seem fine.

173
09:09.446 --> 09:10.280
Are you okay?

174
09:10.364 --> 09:11.573
[Yi-jun] What if I said I wasn't?

175
09:11.656 --> 09:13.075
-Would you keep this up? -[gasps]

176
09:13.158 --> 09:14.534
[grunts, groans]

177
09:20.290 --> 09:22.626
He keeps screwing me over.

178
09:25.295 --> 09:26.588
[inhales]

179
09:26.671 --> 09:27.964
This won't do.

180
09:29.257 --> 09:31.510
I'm gonna have to straighten him out first.

181
09:32.844 --> 09:33.845
What's taking so long?

182
09:33.929 --> 09:35.389
You fly all the way to Milan to get my…

183
09:35.472 --> 09:36.681
[door closes]

184
09:37.599 --> 09:38.975
Seriously?

185
09:39.851 --> 09:40.852
-[Jae-hee] Huh? -Do you think…

186
09:41.520 --> 09:43.105
that I'm actually gonna wear that?

187
09:43.605 --> 09:44.731
You said you were heading out,

188
09:44.815 --> 09:46.691
so I thought I would pick out a low-key outfit.

189
09:46.775 --> 09:47.984
Low-key?

190
09:48.068 --> 09:49.486
Low-key?

191
09:49.569 --> 09:50.862
Listen up, Army Man.

192
09:50.946 --> 09:52.656
I am the face of the Taekang Group.

193
09:52.739 --> 09:55.492
That means everything that I wear is also the face of Taekang.

194
09:55.575 --> 09:58.912
You think I should wear this clown suit and parade around town like a maniac?

195
10:00.455 --> 10:01.748
[gasps] Uh…

196
10:02.207 --> 10:03.500
-Forget it. -Uh…

197
10:03.583 --> 10:04.418
Pants first.

198
10:05.168 --> 10:06.086
[sighs]

199
10:12.968 --> 10:13.802
What are you doing?

200
10:13.885 --> 10:16.221
I'm being your human clothing rack, sir.

201
10:16.304 --> 10:17.764
I get that,

202
10:17.848 --> 10:20.267
but I wanna know why my rack is facing away.

203
10:22.310 --> 10:23.520
[gulps]

204
10:27.190 --> 10:28.817
I don't know what your deal is.

205
10:33.947 --> 10:35.449
-You a prude? -I mean…

206
10:35.532 --> 10:37.200
even between two guys,

207
10:37.284 --> 10:39.035
there's still a thing called personal space.

208
10:39.119 --> 10:40.120
Sir, when you just…

209
10:40.203 --> 10:42.539
casually whip off your clothes, it…

210
10:42.622 --> 10:43.665
Oh, this is stupid.

211
10:44.875 --> 10:45.750
What's the problem?

212
10:46.209 --> 10:47.085
You were fine earlier.

213
10:47.169 --> 10:48.128
Ugh, I didn't…

214
10:51.047 --> 10:52.299
I didn't look on purpose.

215
10:52.924 --> 10:54.634
I was just checking if you were hurt.

216
10:54.718 --> 10:57.387
I'm sure you and your squad mates used to change together.

217
10:57.471 --> 10:58.555
Am I right?

218
10:59.055 --> 10:59.890
Next time, you do it.

219
11:00.390 --> 11:01.433
[rattling effect]

220
11:01.516 --> 11:02.601
It's only fair.

221
11:11.359 --> 11:14.488
[gentle music playing]

222
11:19.993 --> 11:20.869
[gasps]

223
11:26.750 --> 11:27.876
What are you doing, sir?

224
11:53.401 --> 11:54.528
What are you, a child?

225
11:55.070 --> 11:56.530
Can't you put on a tie properly?

226
12:04.204 --> 12:07.374
I was going to pay your hospital bill, but you seem fine.

227
12:07.457 --> 12:08.792
[Yi-jun] Who are you?

228
12:08.875 --> 12:10.126
Who sent you?

229
12:12.337 --> 12:14.256
Gonna see if I was hurt yesterday-- [grunts]

230
12:16.174 --> 12:17.592
You weren't, so forget it.

231
12:22.097 --> 12:22.931
[gasps]

232
12:23.014 --> 12:26.142
[Jae-hee] So, uh… where are you headed, sir?

233
12:27.727 --> 12:28.728
[Yi-jun] This place.

234
12:47.247 --> 12:48.498
[clears throat]

235
12:49.833 --> 12:50.834
Pardon me, sir.

236
12:51.376 --> 12:52.502
I checked the camera,

237
12:52.586 --> 12:54.754
and it only had photos from when you left the house

238
12:54.838 --> 12:56.047
to when you got to the art center.

239
12:57.090 --> 12:59.426
I'll look into the reporter, then decide what to do.

240
12:59.509 --> 13:01.469
Let him be. I know him.

241
13:03.054 --> 13:04.014
You know him, sir?

242
13:11.354 --> 13:14.983
EXECUTIVE DIRECTOR YOON NA-JUNG

243
13:15.900 --> 13:18.361
[breathes deeply]

244
13:18.987 --> 13:20.780
-[door opens, closes] -[gasps]

245
13:21.197 --> 13:23.450
-[Na-jung] He got caught? [huffs] -Oh.

246
13:25.035 --> 13:26.077
What did I tell you?

247
13:26.161 --> 13:27.329
I told you Yi-jun's not an easy--

248
13:27.412 --> 13:29.247
Your man couldn't even follow the punk.

249
13:29.331 --> 13:30.248
Fire him!

250
13:30.749 --> 13:32.792
If I do that, what if word gets around

251
13:32.876 --> 13:35.253
that the company CEO was spying on his own people?

252
13:35.337 --> 13:36.254
Honey.

253
13:36.338 --> 13:37.422
Uh-huh?

254
13:37.505 --> 13:39.341
Think of the shareholder meeting.

255
13:39.424 --> 13:40.800
I know, I know.

256
13:40.884 --> 13:42.969
Would Yi-jun have done that with the shareholder meeting

257
13:43.053 --> 13:44.012
right around the corner though?

258
13:44.095 --> 13:47.515
It actually doesn't matter if he killed anyone.

259
13:47.599 --> 13:49.809
True. What matters more are your dad's intentions.

260
13:50.268 --> 13:52.771
I get that a crisis for Yi-jun could be a good thing,

261
13:52.854 --> 13:55.357
but your dad seemed intent on sweeping this under the rug.

262
13:56.399 --> 13:57.400
Well, he can't.

263
13:58.234 --> 13:59.069
What?

264
14:03.073 --> 14:06.451
Our dear Chairman Yoon really knows how to work the numbers.

265
14:07.369 --> 14:09.204
But if he stands to lose something,

266
14:09.621 --> 14:11.915
not even his children are safe from him.

267
14:11.998 --> 14:15.001
Honey, just tell me what the heck you're thinking.

268
14:16.127 --> 14:18.588
You know that new personal secretary of his?

269
14:22.676 --> 14:24.928
I think it's about time I met up with him.

270
14:26.680 --> 14:27.681
[chuckles]

271
14:45.365 --> 14:47.283
[Jae-hee] Yoon Yi-jun's visiting a columbarium.

272
14:48.660 --> 14:50.495
Could he be here for Han Eun-young?

273
15:19.023 --> 15:22.610
OUR DEAREST DAUGHTER

274
15:22.694 --> 15:24.320
HAN EUN-YOUNG

275
15:35.290 --> 15:38.042
Yoon Yi-jun, what are you thinking?

276
15:39.919 --> 15:42.255
[Captain Park] Why on earth would he come to visit a columbarium?

277
15:42.338 --> 15:45.091
I wonder what the heck's going on inside that prick's head.

278
15:45.175 --> 15:47.385
I used to attend criminal profiling lectures,

279
15:48.011 --> 15:49.554
and speaking from a profiling standpoint,

280
15:49.637 --> 15:51.222
-he-- -Detective Kim, what do you think?

281
15:52.432 --> 15:54.017
Though we'd need an expert opinion,

282
15:54.100 --> 15:56.895
perpetrators have been known to develop PTSD from their crimes,

283
15:56.978 --> 15:58.730
then blaming their victims for it.

284
15:59.731 --> 16:02.192
These feelings stem from a sense of having lost control

285
16:02.275 --> 16:03.401
when things don't go to plan.

286
16:03.485 --> 16:05.195
-Exactly. So, so that loss of-- -Shh!

287
16:05.695 --> 16:06.571
And then?

288
16:07.238 --> 16:10.867
Or he's trying to compensate for the guilt he feels due to cognitive dissonance.

289
16:10.950 --> 16:12.035
Hmm.

290
16:12.118 --> 16:14.996
May also be a defense mechanism seen in high-functioning sociopaths.

291
16:16.289 --> 16:18.958
Great. Wan-gu, did you have some thoughts you wanted to add?

292
16:19.042 --> 16:20.585
-Me? My thoughts? -Uh-huh.

293
16:20.668 --> 16:21.753
[bell chiming effect]

294
16:21.836 --> 16:23.046
Here's what I think.

295
16:23.129 --> 16:25.256
Why else would he feel sorry about it?

296
16:25.340 --> 16:26.716
Because they were seeing each other.

297
16:26.800 --> 16:27.884
Mm, so you said.

298
16:29.219 --> 16:31.763
Anyway, I'm sure the cracks will start showing

299
16:31.846 --> 16:33.264
now that he's facing the deceased.

300
16:33.348 --> 16:34.974
We'll have to catch him when his guard is down.

301
16:35.058 --> 16:36.309
Keep an eye on him.

302
16:40.104 --> 16:40.939
[sighs]

303
16:41.022 --> 16:42.065
ALL RECORDED FILES

304
16:42.607 --> 16:43.775
[footsteps approaching]

305
16:43.858 --> 16:44.692
[chimes]

306
16:47.111 --> 16:49.781
[bird cawing]

307
16:53.743 --> 16:55.578
Sir, wasn't she your secretary?

308
17:00.124 --> 17:01.084
That's right.

309
17:02.210 --> 17:03.628
You must have cared for her.

310
17:04.170 --> 17:05.839
It's a long way to come for a visit.

311
17:05.922 --> 17:07.173
I wanted to apologize.

312
17:08.633 --> 17:09.926
Apologize for what?

313
17:11.219 --> 17:13.221
Well, I'm the reason she's dead.

314
17:13.888 --> 17:15.974
[Jae-hee] Is he admitting his guilt right now?

315
17:16.057 --> 17:17.809
I need him to be more specific.

316
17:17.892 --> 17:19.644
I'm not sure I understand, sir.

317
17:20.228 --> 17:22.063
Are you saying you killed her, Mr. Yoon?

318
17:22.146 --> 17:24.524
[tense music playing]

319
17:27.569 --> 17:28.570
You.

320
17:29.112 --> 17:30.572
What's with all the questions?

321
17:30.655 --> 17:32.824
What are you getting at, Mr. Soldier Boy?

322
17:35.785 --> 17:38.246
You knew what you were getting into on the day of the interview.

323
17:38.329 --> 17:41.040
What? Don't tell me you're getting cold feet.

324
17:41.124 --> 17:42.667
You worried that could happen to you?

325
17:48.172 --> 17:49.799
If you're so scared, just quit.

326
17:50.717 --> 17:51.926
I won't stop you.

327
17:55.555 --> 17:57.056
I am not quitting.

328
17:59.142 --> 18:00.602
I'll stand by your side, sir.

329
18:02.520 --> 18:04.063
[Yi-jun] What's with all the questions?

330
18:04.147 --> 18:06.107
What are you getting at, Mr. Soldier Boy?

331
18:07.108 --> 18:08.943
Don't tell me you're getting cold feet.

332
18:09.027 --> 18:10.737
You worried that could happen to you?

333
18:10.820 --> 18:11.946
He fell for it.

334
18:12.030 --> 18:13.656
Hey, we got it. Let's go!

335
18:13.740 --> 18:14.699
Hey, get a move on!

336
18:14.782 --> 18:16.034
What are we waiting for?

337
18:16.117 --> 18:18.077
'Cause this is illegally obtained evidence.

338
18:18.161 --> 18:20.204
[groans] I know. You think I don't know that?

339
18:20.288 --> 18:23.166
But if we just nab him and grill him good,

340
18:23.249 --> 18:24.834
just put him in a room with Kang, and beat--

341
18:24.918 --> 18:27.545
The problem is, is that it's a matter of criminal procedure.

342
18:27.629 --> 18:29.923
This evidence wouldn't hold up in court. Don't you get it?

343
18:30.757 --> 18:31.799
Kinda.

344
18:31.883 --> 18:32.884
[sighs]

345
18:33.426 --> 18:34.260
[sighs]

346
18:34.344 --> 18:35.178
Dang.

347
18:36.429 --> 18:38.139
[superior] Fine, go fill up your schedule.

348
18:38.222 --> 18:39.641
Get some evidence, or…

349
18:40.475 --> 18:42.018
you are really gonna get it.

350
18:42.101 --> 18:43.102
[sighs]

351
18:43.895 --> 18:45.855
We can't afford to wait for her to find the phone.

352
18:46.606 --> 18:48.608
-That prick, Mr. Park. -Should we summon him?

353
18:52.362 --> 18:56.115
[engine revving]

354
19:06.834 --> 19:07.794
Go home now.

355
19:08.544 --> 19:10.421
It's not time for me to go home yet.

356
19:10.505 --> 19:11.839
I said go.

357
19:19.764 --> 19:20.848
[Ms. Choi] Mr. Kang.

358
19:23.184 --> 19:25.645
When Mr. Yoon is like that, just give him space.

359
19:26.354 --> 19:30.024
I, uh, used to work at his family home and followed him when he moved.

360
19:30.984 --> 19:33.820
I get why he ended up with such a cold disposition.

361
19:34.487 --> 19:36.489
Your home should feel like one.

362
19:36.572 --> 19:40.660
The chairman was always strict, but ever since his wife's unusual death…

363
19:40.743 --> 19:41.911
[gasps]

364
19:45.456 --> 19:47.041
Oh, um, that's confidential.

365
19:47.750 --> 19:49.502
I'm sure you signed an NDA as well.

366
19:50.003 --> 19:51.295
Pretend you didn't hear that.

367
19:51.379 --> 19:52.213
Mm.

368
19:52.839 --> 19:55.174
Or it may not turn out well for you. Got it?

369
19:55.258 --> 19:57.677
-Uh, yes. -[Ms. Choi chuckles awkwardly]

370
19:57.760 --> 20:00.638
Hey, uh, does anyone ever visit Mr. Yoon?

371
20:00.722 --> 20:02.724
Any friends or family come around?

372
20:02.807 --> 20:04.684
Mr. Kim's the only person I've met who's been here.

373
20:04.767 --> 20:07.478
Mm-hmm. Mr. Yoon doesn't really care for visitors.

374
20:09.063 --> 20:12.400
Although his older sister did occasionally drop by,

375
20:13.109 --> 20:14.861
but I guess she's busy nowadays.

376
20:15.778 --> 20:17.113
[Ms. Choi chuckles]

377
20:17.196 --> 20:18.406
By the way, Mr. Kang…

378
20:25.913 --> 20:26.956
do you have a girlfriend?

379
20:27.040 --> 20:27.915
What?

380
20:27.999 --> 20:29.417
What kind of girl do you like?

381
20:30.043 --> 20:31.711
It's just that I have three daughters and…

382
20:31.794 --> 20:34.088
Well, they're all pretty like me.

383
20:34.172 --> 20:35.381
Oh, uh…

384
20:35.465 --> 20:36.674
My, you seem excited.

385
20:36.758 --> 20:37.633
-Not at all. -Huh?

386
20:37.717 --> 20:39.177
-Uh… -Oh, just humor me.

387
20:39.260 --> 20:40.344
-I wasn't excited. -Okay?

388
20:40.428 --> 20:42.597
-Just pick one of them for me. -[sighs]

389
20:53.316 --> 20:54.901
[Yi-jun] I wanted to apologize.

390
20:56.235 --> 20:57.904
Well, I'm the reason she's dead.

391
20:58.696 --> 21:00.698
[pensive music playing]

392
21:01.365 --> 21:03.201
Don't tell me you're getting cold feet.

393
21:03.910 --> 21:05.578
You worried that could happen to you?

394
21:06.287 --> 21:07.538
[sighs]

395
21:08.164 --> 21:09.582
[panting]

396
21:23.096 --> 21:26.516
I was going to pay your hospital bill, but you seem fine.

397
21:33.314 --> 21:34.315
[sighs]

398
21:43.658 --> 21:45.451
SAESUPGIL HAEJANGGUK

399
21:47.078 --> 21:49.747
[Hye-jung] Auntie, can I get a large haejangguk?

400
21:52.834 --> 21:56.170
Goodness, you should give the bottle a rest, eh?

401
21:56.254 --> 21:58.923
One might think you're a woman with a tragic backstory.

402
21:59.382 --> 22:02.301
What's a girl like you doing coming to a place like this

403
22:02.385 --> 22:05.138
and throwing a pity party for yourself every day?

404
22:05.221 --> 22:07.140
Everyone has a tragic backstory.

405
22:07.723 --> 22:08.558
You too?

406
22:09.600 --> 22:10.685
I do.

407
22:13.896 --> 22:14.981
You see…

408
22:16.232 --> 22:18.860
I've got this really big secret weighing me down.

409
22:19.360 --> 22:21.195
-What is it? -[Hye-jung] Get this.

410
22:22.780 --> 22:24.740
She's going to have an accident and die.

411
22:25.241 --> 22:26.409
[actress] …Gyeong-ho who did it?

412
22:26.993 --> 22:27.910
-I don't believe it. -[store owner] Hey!

413
22:27.994 --> 22:29.412
I haven't made it that far yet.

414
22:29.912 --> 22:31.122
And that's the very reason

415
22:31.205 --> 22:33.291
why you shouldn't pry into other people's secrets.

416
22:33.374 --> 22:34.208
[store owner] Oh?

417
22:34.792 --> 22:35.626
Look at her.

418
22:36.586 --> 22:38.796
She went digging only to end up dead.

419
22:38.880 --> 22:41.174
[tense music sting]

420
22:43.467 --> 22:44.510
[store owner] Oh…

421
22:45.595 --> 22:46.554
Oh my.

422
22:55.188 --> 22:56.063
[Yi-jun] Ms. Han.

423
22:56.522 --> 22:57.815
-[thunder rumbling] -Ms. Han!

424
22:58.482 --> 22:59.483
Ms. Han!

425
23:00.318 --> 23:01.736
-[thunder rumbling] -[gasps]

426
23:01.819 --> 23:04.155
[gasping]

427
23:07.033 --> 23:08.117
[exhales shakily]

428
23:08.492 --> 23:11.704
[panting]

429
23:14.999 --> 23:18.794
[phone ringing]

430
23:22.965 --> 23:25.384
-[ringing continues] -[groans]

431
23:26.802 --> 23:27.637
MR. YOON YI-JUN

432
23:29.013 --> 23:30.681
[clearing throat]

433
23:31.474 --> 23:32.433
Yeah, hello?

434
23:34.810 --> 23:35.686
Huh?

435
23:36.687 --> 23:38.689
What? [sighs]

436
23:42.068 --> 23:43.319
[tires screeching]

437
23:44.737 --> 23:46.072
[Jae-hee] Thank you very much.

438
23:48.199 --> 23:49.158
[beeps, chimes]

439
23:49.700 --> 23:51.369
What's going on? [panting]

440
23:51.911 --> 23:52.828
[Jae-hee] Hmm…

441
23:54.497 --> 23:55.331
[Jae-hee inhales]

442
23:55.414 --> 23:58.793
All right, so what you're telling me is you drank from this bottle yesterday,

443
23:58.876 --> 24:02.380
and the milk in the bottle you drank from has increased by 10 mL?

444
24:03.130 --> 24:04.173
Yeah, that's right.

445
24:04.257 --> 24:05.508
This is a one-liter bottle.

446
24:05.591 --> 24:07.969
I drank 250 mL, right?

447
24:08.344 --> 24:09.220
What should that leave me with?

448
24:13.224 --> 24:16.227
Did you measure exactly 250 when you poured it?

449
24:18.145 --> 24:19.146
I didn't.

450
24:19.230 --> 24:21.232
Did you check to see how much you actually drank?

451
24:21.315 --> 24:22.483
I didn't.

452
24:22.566 --> 24:25.403
Then how can you be so sure that you drank exactly 250?

453
24:25.486 --> 24:28.447
When I held the glass in my hand, I could tell the difference right then,

454
24:28.531 --> 24:31.284
so wouldn't that mean something was added to it?

455
24:31.367 --> 24:34.287
This is why you made a huge deal as if something terrible happened

456
24:34.370 --> 24:36.372
-and told me to rush over here? -What could be worse than this?

457
24:37.164 --> 24:38.791
You said you'd stand by my side.

458
24:38.874 --> 24:40.001
Did you mean it?

459
24:41.294 --> 24:42.545
[scoffs]

460
24:42.628 --> 24:44.672
Throw them all out. They feel off.

461
24:46.090 --> 24:47.800
Did I really say that?

462
24:47.883 --> 24:49.135
[Yi-jun] If you're so scared, just quit.

463
24:49.969 --> 24:50.928
I won't stop you.

464
24:54.390 --> 24:55.266
I am not quitting.

465
24:57.393 --> 24:58.936
I'll stand by your side, sir.

466
25:03.733 --> 25:04.900
Why's that?

467
25:10.740 --> 25:11.657
I need the money.

468
25:12.533 --> 25:14.535
And no one else pays as much money as you do…

469
25:15.119 --> 25:15.995
Mr. Yoon.

470
25:23.753 --> 25:25.129
[warbling effect]

471
25:25.796 --> 25:26.964
I guess I did.

472
25:27.048 --> 25:27.882
[inhales]

473
25:28.758 --> 25:32.553
Which is why I expect you to earn your keep, yeah?

474
25:35.389 --> 25:36.557
I'm going to sleep.

475
25:37.600 --> 25:39.268
Right, so good night, sir.

476
25:39.352 --> 25:40.311
I'll head home then.

477
25:42.396 --> 25:44.148
I said I'm going to bed now.

478
25:45.149 --> 25:46.650
[Jae-hee] So what do you need?

479
25:46.734 --> 25:50.321
Well, I'm not sleeping very well, and now I can't even drink milk to help.

480
25:50.946 --> 25:51.864
What should I do?

481
25:52.406 --> 25:54.241
[Jae-hee] How much longer do I have to let this idiot

482
25:54.325 --> 25:56.243
wake me up in the middle of the night?

483
25:56.327 --> 25:57.953
Just keep me safe until I'm asleep.

484
25:58.037 --> 25:59.372
[frustrated groan]

485
25:59.455 --> 26:00.831
[Jae-hee] Hold on.

486
26:00.915 --> 26:02.541
Once he's asleep, I could…

487
26:03.667 --> 26:04.877
check out that room.

488
26:07.588 --> 26:08.422
[gasps]

489
26:09.340 --> 26:10.341
Understood, sir.

490
26:10.883 --> 26:12.885
I'll stand by your side until you fall asleep.

491
26:15.513 --> 26:16.764
I'll keep you safe, sir.

492
26:18.516 --> 26:19.350
Let's go.

493
26:20.309 --> 26:22.353
-Here. Let's go. -Uh, wait, I…

494
26:22.436 --> 26:23.604
Good night. Let's go.

495
26:23.687 --> 26:24.980
-What about the milk? -Hurry along now.

496
26:25.064 --> 26:27.483
[narrator] Her role was not that of a trained commander,

497
26:27.983 --> 26:30.653
but her presence carried symbolic force.

498
26:31.445 --> 26:35.408
At the Siege of Orléans, French morale was restored,

499
26:35.908 --> 26:38.369
and the course of the war began to shift.

500
26:39.495 --> 26:41.122
Do you like documentaries, sir?

501
26:41.205 --> 26:45.209
She distinguished herself in many battles, and even led her side to victory.

502
26:45.876 --> 26:47.253
So you're a history geek.

503
26:47.336 --> 26:48.712
She was such an inspiration.

504
26:48.796 --> 26:51.173
In France, there's even a statue of her on horseback,

505
26:51.257 --> 26:52.633
making her triumphant return.

506
26:53.008 --> 26:54.260
But isn't it amazing?

507
26:54.343 --> 26:55.719
They say despite her heroics,

508
26:55.803 --> 26:56.762
she went around

509
26:56.846 --> 26:59.098
disguised as a man right up to the end.

510
27:04.395 --> 27:06.063
So you're actually a hero geek.

511
27:06.689 --> 27:08.107
But Mr. Yoon… [sighs]

512
27:08.190 --> 27:09.567
…at this rate, we'll stay up all night.

513
27:10.860 --> 27:11.777
Let's go to your bedroom.

514
27:13.612 --> 27:14.572
[Jerry meows]

515
27:15.948 --> 27:17.283
Did you know about Atalanta?

516
27:17.366 --> 27:18.617
I didn't, sir.

517
27:21.787 --> 27:24.248
She was the greatest archer in Greco-Roman mythology.

518
27:25.040 --> 27:27.084
Would you by chance like to spar with me, sir?

519
27:27.626 --> 27:30.546
I can make sure you're out cold for the rest of the night.

520
27:32.506 --> 27:33.340
[Jerry hisses]

521
27:41.557 --> 27:43.642
[Jerry purring]

522
27:44.518 --> 27:45.978
I hate working up a sweat.

523
27:46.562 --> 27:47.855
[Yi-jun chuckles]

524
27:48.564 --> 27:50.065
Even he knows I feel that way,

525
27:50.149 --> 27:53.819
so how could my personal secretary not know that? [tuts]

526
27:54.320 --> 27:55.905
[Jae-hee] I don't care about your feelings.

527
27:56.405 --> 27:57.656
Just go to sleep.

528
27:58.407 --> 27:59.617
Although…

529
28:00.075 --> 28:01.076
it is strange.

530
28:02.536 --> 28:05.498
Dear Jerry here has always been partial to men.

531
28:06.081 --> 28:07.541
At least that was the case with Kim Si-hyun

532
28:07.625 --> 28:09.752
and that ungrateful Mr. Jung.

533
28:13.005 --> 28:16.217
And yet, it appears you're the only one he despises.

534
28:16.300 --> 28:17.426
[gulps]

535
28:18.719 --> 28:19.553
Right, Jerry?

536
28:20.554 --> 28:22.556
[low growling]

537
28:22.640 --> 28:23.474
[knife whooshing effect]

538
28:26.268 --> 28:28.395
Our dear Army Man here…

539
28:31.565 --> 28:34.360
seems extraordinarily beneath you, doesn't he?

540
28:35.653 --> 28:37.571
-[Jae-hee sighs] -[meows]

541
28:39.281 --> 28:40.866
[Yi-jun] Yes, you're right.

542
28:40.950 --> 28:42.618
-Gosh, you're so smart. -[hisses]

543
28:42.701 --> 28:44.453
Hmm? [chuckles]

544
28:54.171 --> 28:56.340
Hey, kitty cat, come over here.

545
28:56.423 --> 28:57.299
[Jerry meows]

546
28:57.841 --> 28:58.717
[Jae-hee] Come here.

547
28:59.635 --> 29:01.845
It's lactose-free, so you can drink it.

548
29:02.471 --> 29:03.931
Super expensive.

549
29:04.014 --> 29:04.848
Drink it up.

550
29:05.599 --> 29:07.351
Sheesh, I told you to drink the milk.

551
29:07.851 --> 29:11.897
Also, if you keep acting all jumpy, he'll trust me less, huh?

552
29:12.606 --> 29:14.942
So from here on out, let's try to get along.

553
29:15.025 --> 29:16.026
Hmm? Deal?

554
29:18.529 --> 29:21.240
[low growling]

555
29:21.323 --> 29:23.409
Huh? Why are you glaring at me?

556
29:24.910 --> 29:25.911
[meows]

557
29:29.039 --> 29:31.417
[calm voice] Treat yourself to a comfortable night

558
29:31.500 --> 29:33.627
-for a hard day's work. -[tranquil music playing]

559
29:33.711 --> 29:37.256
This meditation aims to ease you into deep sleep

560
29:37.339 --> 29:41.260
through breathing exercises that will relax your body and mind.

561
29:41.343 --> 29:42.595
-No yawning. -[yawns]

562
29:46.473 --> 29:48.017
Mr. Yoon, I'm only human.

563
29:48.100 --> 29:49.852
I did drive you around all day, you know?

564
29:50.436 --> 29:53.147
On top of that, I took a Korean listening evaluation.

565
29:53.230 --> 29:55.065
I'll have to go home after you fall asleep,

566
29:55.149 --> 29:56.483
then come back to work again.

567
29:56.900 --> 29:58.652
-Of course I'm a little tired. -[sucks teeth]

568
29:58.736 --> 29:59.570
[Yi-jun] Shh!

569
30:01.488 --> 30:02.740
I'll stop yawning.

570
30:03.324 --> 30:04.908
[yawns] Poof!

571
30:06.994 --> 30:10.164
-[guide] Your body and mind are relaxing. -[breathes softly]

572
30:10.247 --> 30:11.206
[hisses]

573
30:11.290 --> 30:12.583
[Jae-hee] I was breathing.

574
30:12.666 --> 30:14.335
-[guide] With every exhale… -[meows]

575
30:14.418 --> 30:17.129
…release all the tension in your body.

576
30:17.212 --> 30:18.881
-[Jae-hee snoring] -[music stops]

577
30:23.177 --> 30:26.388
[comical music playing]

578
30:29.141 --> 30:30.309
[Yi-jun clears throat loudly]

579
30:39.860 --> 30:41.111
[Jae-hee snoring]

580
30:41.195 --> 30:42.780
-[inhales deeply] -[claps]

581
30:54.500 --> 30:55.501
[soft chuckle]

582
30:56.210 --> 30:58.629
[gentle music playing]

583
31:01.215 --> 31:02.341
-[gasps] -[music stops]

584
31:04.426 --> 31:06.345
I don't like it. [gasps]

585
31:07.971 --> 31:09.890
Everything about you is too weird.

586
31:09.973 --> 31:11.809
[Yi-jun breathing shakily]

587
31:20.234 --> 31:22.736
[soft quirky music playing]

588
31:39.837 --> 31:42.339
[low tense music playing]

589
31:46.260 --> 31:47.386
[beeps, chimes]

590
31:54.643 --> 31:55.686
[Ms. Choi] Mr. Kang?

591
31:59.148 --> 32:00.149
Mr. Kang.

592
32:01.525 --> 32:02.401
Mr. Kang.

593
32:02.484 --> 32:03.318
[gasps]

594
32:03.402 --> 32:04.945
[Jae-hee groaning]

595
32:06.739 --> 32:08.866
Goodness, why were you sleeping here?

596
32:10.701 --> 32:13.078
Huh? Um, what am I doing here?

597
32:13.162 --> 32:14.955
How would I know?

598
32:15.038 --> 32:17.082
I was just as surprised as you.

599
32:17.166 --> 32:18.000
[gasps]

600
32:18.792 --> 32:19.668
Where's Mr. Yoon?

601
32:19.752 --> 32:23.005
-Mm… in his bedroom, I suppose. -[sighs]

602
32:27.134 --> 32:29.595
Uh, I… I'll get ready for work and be right back.

603
32:33.557 --> 32:35.350
[breathing heavily]

604
32:38.771 --> 32:39.605
Hey.

605
32:41.982 --> 32:43.692
Ugh, that damn cat.

606
32:44.443 --> 32:46.570
He's a picky eater, like his owner.

607
32:49.782 --> 32:51.742
[suspenseful music playing]

608
32:53.327 --> 32:54.244
What?

609
32:55.162 --> 32:56.705
[Jae-hee] What's up with this milk?

610
32:57.289 --> 32:58.665
It turned the bowl black.

611
32:59.708 --> 33:02.628
When I held the glass in my hand, I could tell the difference right then,

612
33:02.711 --> 33:05.756
so wouldn't that mean something was added to it?

613
33:08.467 --> 33:09.551
[Ms. Choi] This way, please.

614
33:14.473 --> 33:15.474
[Jerry meows]

615
33:19.561 --> 33:20.813
[low growling]

616
33:20.896 --> 33:21.730
[hisses]

617
33:42.459 --> 33:45.504
[eerie music sting]

618
33:50.551 --> 33:54.054
[Jae-hee] Something strange is going on in this house.

619
34:09.444 --> 34:11.655
Let's see. I'll go this way,

620
34:11.738 --> 34:13.198
-and you go that way, okay? -Yes, sir.

621
34:13.282 --> 34:14.366
Go.

622
34:41.810 --> 34:44.229
[Captain Park] "251YI3108."

623
34:44.313 --> 34:45.939
[panting] Captain.

624
34:51.403 --> 34:52.946
-Not there? -No.

625
34:53.447 --> 34:55.073
And it seems he may have been gone a while.

626
34:55.157 --> 34:56.283
Where could he be?

627
34:57.200 --> 34:59.494
So he ditched his car, and now we can't find him anywhere.

628
34:59.578 --> 35:01.163
-[phone buzzes] -We'll see if we can track him down.

629
35:01.246 --> 35:02.205
Where was the management office?

630
35:02.289 --> 35:05.250
[Jae-hee] Mr. Kim, come to Yoon Yi-jun's house right now.

631
35:05.876 --> 35:07.294
Detective Kang needs me over there.

632
35:07.377 --> 35:09.713
Why? She get into trouble?

633
35:20.223 --> 35:22.684
-[eerie music sting] -[phone buzzing]

634
35:26.313 --> 35:27.898
Let's go out for soju another time.

635
35:27.981 --> 35:29.274
Someone around you?

636
35:29.775 --> 35:32.444
Oh, I just don't think I can make it to see you today.

637
35:33.111 --> 35:34.029
[Seok-jin] Are you in danger?

638
35:34.529 --> 35:35.572
I'll be there in three minutes.

639
35:36.073 --> 35:36.907
Oh, that's right.

640
35:36.990 --> 35:38.533
Did you get my email?

641
35:38.617 --> 35:39.826
The mailbox?

642
35:39.910 --> 35:40.953
Yeah.

643
35:41.036 --> 35:42.537
Look, I'm kind of busy right now,

644
35:43.121 --> 35:45.082
but I'll keep an eye out for your reply.

645
35:45.582 --> 35:46.708
Don't worry. I got it.

646
35:46.792 --> 35:48.377
Hey, are you okay?

647
35:48.460 --> 35:49.962
Yeah, of course, Hyung.

648
35:50.045 --> 35:53.340
-Good. Don't make me worry about you. -[dramatic music rises]

649
35:53.423 --> 35:54.675
-[music stops] -I won't.

650
35:55.258 --> 35:58.136
[upbeat intense music playing]

651
36:17.072 --> 36:18.532
[panting]

652
36:20.283 --> 36:21.284
Huh?

653
36:27.332 --> 36:29.001
[panting]

654
36:33.422 --> 36:34.423
[Jae-hee grunts]

655
36:35.048 --> 36:36.925
[grunting]

656
36:37.009 --> 36:38.051
[lurker] No, wait!

657
36:38.135 --> 36:39.636
-Hold on, hold on! [groans] -[joints crack]

658
36:40.137 --> 36:42.431
Hold on, I'm Mr. Jung! I'm Mr. Jung!

659
36:45.183 --> 36:46.435
What are you up to?

660
36:47.769 --> 36:49.354
[screams in pain]

661
36:49.438 --> 36:51.398
[groaning, sobbing]

662
36:52.774 --> 36:55.736
"Without knowing that outside may be bitterly cold…"

663
36:55.819 --> 36:56.653
LETTER OF APOLOGY

664
36:56.737 --> 36:58.196
"…with winter snowstorms raging…"

665
36:58.280 --> 36:59.114
[yawns]

666
37:00.741 --> 37:03.577
"…I, who have grown up pampered, like a greenhouse flower,

667
37:03.660 --> 37:06.788
and thanks to your love, I've become far too complacent."

668
37:06.872 --> 37:07.998
[Da-woon] Mr. Yoon!

669
37:08.874 --> 37:11.710
My kid's entering a private kindergarten.

670
37:11.793 --> 37:13.837
[comical music playing]

671
37:13.920 --> 37:15.547
If I were to go home right now,

672
37:16.381 --> 37:17.799
my wife would beat me to death.

673
37:19.301 --> 37:20.510
Have some mercy.

674
37:20.594 --> 37:23.805
Not long ago, you threw a letter of resignation in my face,

675
37:23.889 --> 37:26.141
and now you're begging to get your job back?

676
37:26.224 --> 37:28.393
I would never throw something in the face of a king.

677
37:29.811 --> 37:33.065
That letter that I so gently placed in your delicate, soft hands…

678
37:33.815 --> 37:35.734
could you please tear it up just this once?

679
37:36.193 --> 37:37.027
[scoffs]

680
37:37.110 --> 37:38.236
[squeaking effect]

681
37:39.988 --> 37:40.822
You.

682
37:42.866 --> 37:44.868
You said you'd keep me safe while I slept.

683
37:44.951 --> 37:45.994
Why'd you go outside?

684
37:46.912 --> 37:49.289
I was patrolling the inner and outer perimeter, sir.

685
37:49.372 --> 37:51.792
-Patrolling? -I kept a proper watch, sir.

686
37:52.292 --> 37:54.586
So I could ensure you got a good night's rest.

687
37:54.669 --> 37:59.299
Ah… so you captured Mr. Jung by keeping a proper watch, huh?

688
37:59.382 --> 38:01.426
Does keeping a proper watch include falling asleep

689
38:01.510 --> 38:04.221
before I did, Mr. Special Forces?

690
38:04.721 --> 38:05.555
[gasps]

691
38:05.639 --> 38:06.932
You're the one who woke me up

692
38:07.015 --> 38:08.391
in the middle of the night out of nowhere, sir.

693
38:08.975 --> 38:10.936
I'm afraid my hours mentioned in the contract

694
38:11.019 --> 38:13.105
didn't cover any extra early morning shifts.

695
38:13.188 --> 38:14.564
That's why I didn't wake you up.

696
38:14.648 --> 38:15.816
[bird hooting effect]

697
38:17.192 --> 38:20.028
You… were sleeping so well.

698
38:20.112 --> 38:21.279
You were having one sweet sleep.

699
38:21.363 --> 38:22.906
Why didn't you wake me up then?

700
38:22.989 --> 38:24.491
You always get the last word in.

701
38:24.574 --> 38:26.326
-In that case, I'll add one more thing. -[Yi-jun] Don't do it.

702
38:26.409 --> 38:27.994
I'm warning you, don't do it.

703
38:28.078 --> 38:29.037
-Do-- -My cab fare!

704
38:29.121 --> 38:31.289
-I'll charge you for it, sir. -Ha? [gasps]

705
38:34.042 --> 38:35.043
[incredulous scoff]

706
38:35.752 --> 38:37.087
-[Yi-jun scoffs] -[nervous chuckle]

707
38:42.843 --> 38:44.678
[Yi-jun] I want the plant consortium proposal

708
38:44.761 --> 38:46.805
by the end of the day, Mr. Gu.

709
38:49.141 --> 38:50.976
It's like they say, people don't change.

710
38:52.060 --> 38:53.061
He's awesome!

711
38:54.354 --> 38:55.188
[Jae-hee] Mr. Jung.

712
38:55.272 --> 38:57.274
Oh, pl-please, it really hurts! Please!

713
38:57.858 --> 38:59.651
Um, you should switch out that tissue.

714
39:00.777 --> 39:01.695
It's grossing me out.

715
39:01.778 --> 39:02.821
Oh…

716
39:03.822 --> 39:04.739
Thanks a lot.

717
39:05.365 --> 39:06.741
So what made you ask to see me?

718
39:06.825 --> 39:07.993
[clears throat]

719
39:08.493 --> 39:09.494
Come with me.

720
39:11.538 --> 39:13.623
[breathes deeply]

721
39:16.209 --> 39:17.460
Hello.

722
39:17.544 --> 39:18.545
[door closes]

723
39:22.591 --> 39:24.926
Mr. Kim Si-hyun from the legal department's here.

724
39:27.387 --> 39:28.388
[handset clacks]

725
39:38.523 --> 39:40.817
CHAIRMAN YOON TAE-SIK

726
39:49.201 --> 39:50.202
[doors close]

727
39:50.952 --> 39:54.998
[Wan-gu] Just as Chairman Yoon Tae-sik is at the center of all power in Taekang…

728
39:55.081 --> 39:56.249
BREAK ROOM

729
39:56.333 --> 39:58.210
…those ladies are at the center

730
39:59.127 --> 40:00.587
of every rumor.

731
40:01.087 --> 40:03.215
Cho Young-sook, the head janitor.

732
40:03.298 --> 40:06.343
Hong Young-chun, the chairman's office janitor.

733
40:06.426 --> 40:08.094
They know all the secrets.

734
40:08.178 --> 40:10.764
They're the ones pulling the strings behind the scenes.

735
40:10.847 --> 40:13.350
-[Young-sook sighs] -They are known as the Young Sisters.

736
40:13.433 --> 40:14.434
[Young-chun] Huh?

737
40:15.018 --> 40:18.146
Mr. Jung from the 32nd floor is making a comeback?

738
40:18.230 --> 40:19.481
[scoffs]

739
40:19.564 --> 40:21.608
Mr. Jung? Hmm?

740
40:21.691 --> 40:23.235
-[Young-chun] Mm? -[Young-sook] Oh, sorry.

741
40:23.318 --> 40:25.445
This is the guy who just joined us on the seventh floor.

742
40:25.528 --> 40:26.905
[Young-chun] Mm…

743
40:26.988 --> 40:29.032
All right, rookie. What am I gonna call you?

744
40:29.616 --> 40:31.868
There are three Bins of note in our nation.

745
40:32.244 --> 40:33.078
Hyun Bin,

746
40:33.161 --> 40:34.037
Won Bin,

747
40:34.120 --> 40:35.789
-and Wan-bin. -[warbling effect]

748
40:35.872 --> 40:37.499
Allow me, Jung Wan-bin,

749
40:37.582 --> 40:39.501
to formally greet you both.

750
40:40.919 --> 40:44.005
[Young-sook] Ah, that mug of yours belongs in a bin if you ask me!

751
40:44.089 --> 40:48.760
Ah, but I wanna know why that slug came crawling back after he resigned.

752
40:48.843 --> 40:52.764
When someone comes crawling back, there can only be one reason for it.

753
40:53.848 --> 40:55.767
Money, money, money.

754
40:55.850 --> 40:58.103
-Money! Mwah! -[cash register dinging effect]

755
40:58.186 --> 40:59.062
[soft gasp]

756
40:59.145 --> 41:01.064
[scoffs] Who knows?

757
41:01.606 --> 41:03.566
Anyway, this just means more work for me.

758
41:04.234 --> 41:08.363
If I ever get my hands around that cheeky, whiny little punk bitch's neck,

759
41:08.446 --> 41:10.490
I'm just gonna mangle that douche!

760
41:10.573 --> 41:12.701
Mr. Jung and her, they don't get along.

761
41:12.784 --> 41:14.452
I think they were enemies in a past life.

762
41:14.536 --> 41:15.453
Ah…

763
41:15.912 --> 41:17.789
Today's her mother-in-law's memorial,

764
41:17.872 --> 41:19.916
but they still called her in to go up and work.

765
41:21.084 --> 41:22.210
The 32nd floor?

766
41:23.503 --> 41:24.379
Ma'am…

767
41:25.046 --> 41:26.965
would you like it if I stepped in?

768
41:27.048 --> 41:28.466
Let me help out.

769
41:29.342 --> 41:30.927
[elevator chimes]

770
41:39.644 --> 41:41.104
You really are ignoring me.

771
41:41.187 --> 41:42.480
I'm hurt.

772
41:48.611 --> 41:50.030
Let's have dinner together.

773
41:50.989 --> 41:52.324
[humming]

774
41:53.616 --> 41:54.451
Hmm?

775
41:56.661 --> 41:58.997
You're just chock-full of surprises, Ms. Lee.

776
41:59.080 --> 42:00.165
Is that a no?

777
42:00.248 --> 42:01.249
Of course not.

778
42:01.833 --> 42:02.917
But what to do?

779
42:03.001 --> 42:04.502
I'm afraid I have a prior engagement.

780
42:04.586 --> 42:06.087
With Mr. Yoon Yi-jun, right?

781
42:06.171 --> 42:09.049
Not only are you full of surprises, but you're also quick.

782
42:09.132 --> 42:11.176
You're making me wanna cancel my appointment.

783
42:12.886 --> 42:14.095
[Si-hyun] Let's meet up tomorrow.

784
42:14.179 --> 42:16.431
[gentle music playing]

785
42:18.016 --> 42:19.309
Let's get something you like.

786
42:19.809 --> 42:20.935
A full-course dinner.

787
42:30.779 --> 42:33.740
[Da-woon] Since it's come to this, we need to get one thing straight.

788
42:35.742 --> 42:38.203
[slurping]

789
42:40.038 --> 42:41.456
[exhales]

790
42:42.374 --> 42:45.126
I'm the top dog, and you serve under me.

791
42:45.877 --> 42:48.338
Whether by work experience or whether by rank,

792
42:48.421 --> 42:50.632
I'm your senior and you're my junior.

793
42:50.715 --> 42:51.591
Clear?

794
42:52.175 --> 42:53.676
Um…

795
42:54.386 --> 42:55.804
Yeah. Sounds good to me.

796
42:56.596 --> 42:58.390
And now that we've gotten that out of the way,

797
42:58.473 --> 42:59.724
why don't we share some secrets?

798
43:00.642 --> 43:01.643
What kind of secrets?

799
43:02.602 --> 43:05.188
How did you get so close to Mr. Yoon in less than a week?

800
43:05.271 --> 43:06.231
[Jae-hee] Whoa.

801
43:06.731 --> 43:08.817
Now why would you say something like that?

802
43:10.568 --> 43:11.778
From what I've seen,

803
43:11.861 --> 43:14.656
he seemed to trust you way more than he trusts me, Mr. Jung.

804
43:14.739 --> 43:16.324
He approved your return to work.

805
43:16.408 --> 43:17.826
[chuckles] Yeah, of course he did.

806
43:17.909 --> 43:19.828
I spent ages working with that man, after all.

807
43:19.911 --> 43:23.164
And is that how you managed to become Mr. Yoon's right-hand man?

808
43:23.248 --> 43:25.792
His right-hand man? [chuckles]

809
43:25.875 --> 43:27.168
[soft chuckle]

810
43:27.252 --> 43:28.920
As his right-hand man,

811
43:29.003 --> 43:30.880
what are your thoughts on Mr. Yoon?

812
43:30.964 --> 43:34.259
I'm afraid I'm… just too inexperienced.

813
43:35.385 --> 43:37.011
-Of course you are. -Mm.

814
43:37.095 --> 43:39.305
I guess I should fill you in as the right-hand man.

815
43:39.389 --> 43:40.598
[Da-woon chuckles]

816
43:41.766 --> 43:44.978
From birth, he was raised to be the successor to Taekang.

817
43:45.645 --> 43:47.939
He cannot shirk a single responsibility.

818
43:48.440 --> 43:52.068
He lives a life of total control in which no mistakes are tolerated.

819
43:56.739 --> 43:58.992
-[secretary] It's the minister, sir. -[sighs]

820
44:01.327 --> 44:04.080
Yes, Minister. This is Yoon Tae-sik.

821
44:04.164 --> 44:06.374
Of course, I'll proceed with things as you said.

822
44:07.083 --> 44:09.210
Thank you, sir. Yes.

823
44:10.545 --> 44:11.463
[phone beeps]

824
44:13.256 --> 44:14.132
[door closes]

825
44:14.215 --> 44:16.384
[tense music sting]

826
44:19.262 --> 44:20.805
This is your best?

827
44:22.557 --> 44:24.184
[Tae-sik] Get your act together!

828
44:24.684 --> 44:27.312
I told you over and over that you're the future of Taekang.

829
44:28.104 --> 44:30.023
[soft sobbing]

830
44:30.565 --> 44:33.359
I'm sorry, Father. [sniffles]

831
44:33.443 --> 44:34.861
I'll try harder.

832
44:34.944 --> 44:36.863
Again with the "I'm sorrys."

833
44:37.655 --> 44:39.157
Do that for another hour.

834
44:45.914 --> 44:46.873
Yes.

835
44:48.625 --> 44:50.376
I'll change it to your preference.

836
44:51.169 --> 44:53.463
Understood. Yeah.

837
44:55.423 --> 44:56.257
[beeps]

838
44:57.884 --> 44:59.385
[sighs]

839
45:00.512 --> 45:02.305
[tense music sting]

840
45:02.388 --> 45:05.141
I can't wait to see how much he's prepared to…

841
45:05.892 --> 45:08.102
screw me over. [breathes shakily]

842
45:12.607 --> 45:15.443
-[Yi-jun] Ms. Han. -[thunder rumbling]

843
45:17.779 --> 45:18.821
Ms. Han.

844
45:19.822 --> 45:22.408
-[gags, grunts] -[tense music playing]

845
45:24.035 --> 45:27.330
-[Yi-jun choking, grunting] -[thunderclap]

846
45:27.413 --> 45:28.331
[gasps]

847
45:28.414 --> 45:30.542
[panting]

848
45:30.625 --> 45:32.252
[Da-woon] Mr. Yoon is perfect.

849
45:33.169 --> 45:34.504
He has to be perfect.

850
45:34.587 --> 45:35.797
[exhales heavily]

851
45:37.840 --> 45:39.926
This is also the reason he's so guarded.

852
45:40.677 --> 45:43.888
Since the name Taekang is attached to everything he does,

853
45:43.972 --> 45:45.723
he can't be easygoing.

854
45:46.224 --> 45:47.475
[sighs]

855
45:52.313 --> 45:54.524
Bet you didn't know he was Taekang's punching bag.

856
45:55.567 --> 45:57.193
He's expected to excel at everything,

857
45:57.277 --> 45:59.320
but people start pointing fingers at the slightest slip-up.

858
46:00.280 --> 46:02.240
People compare him to the chairman back in the day

859
46:02.323 --> 46:03.533
every chance they get,

860
46:03.616 --> 46:05.910
not to mention his rivals who will pounce on him

861
46:05.994 --> 46:08.580
the second they smell weakness. [laughs wryly]

862
46:09.998 --> 46:11.374
No matter how much I think about it,

863
46:11.457 --> 46:13.585
I don't envy that life, except for the money.

864
46:14.335 --> 46:15.837
Mr. Jung, in your opinion…

865
46:17.380 --> 46:18.965
is Mr. Yoon capable of murder?

866
46:21.009 --> 46:21.926
I don't know.

867
46:23.261 --> 46:25.388
He's scary, but I really don't think he'd do it.

868
46:26.931 --> 46:28.850
If I knew he did, I wouldn't have come back here,

869
46:28.933 --> 46:31.060
not even if I had to send my kid to study abroad

870
46:31.144 --> 46:32.895
instead of a private kindergarten.

871
46:34.063 --> 46:35.148
Another thing.

872
46:36.065 --> 46:38.985
About the rumors that Ms. Han and Mr.--

873
46:39.068 --> 46:40.403
Uh-uh. That's totally false.

874
46:41.070 --> 46:42.780
I've been asked that question over 100 times,

875
46:42.864 --> 46:44.866
and no, they weren't dating.

876
46:44.949 --> 46:46.034
They weren't?

877
46:46.117 --> 46:47.869
Beyond a shadow of a doubt, no.

878
46:47.952 --> 46:49.495
How can you be so sure they weren't though?

879
46:51.789 --> 46:55.376
Well, that's because I know Mr. Yoon and Ms. Han's huge secret.

880
46:55.835 --> 46:56.794
Their secret?

881
46:56.878 --> 46:57.795
Mm.

882
46:58.463 --> 47:02.300
Firstly, she had a crush on another guy at the company.

883
47:02.800 --> 47:05.261
Ah, you know, I gave her a lot of dating advice.

884
47:05.345 --> 47:07.138
As for Mr. Yoon, well…

885
47:11.267 --> 47:13.269
-his taste is a bit unusual. -[sighs]

886
47:13.353 --> 47:15.980
-His type of woman is actually-- -Man, I almost took that the wrong way.

887
47:16.064 --> 47:17.231
Never mind, go on.

888
47:17.315 --> 47:18.524
Look, this is your job!

889
47:18.608 --> 47:20.860
You must have a full grasp of Mr. Yoon's tastes and private life

890
47:20.943 --> 47:22.528
so you don't make any mistakes.

891
47:22.945 --> 47:23.946
[sighs]

892
47:24.364 --> 47:26.240
Yeah, of course. Yeah.

893
47:27.033 --> 47:28.785
Continue. What's Mr. Yoon's type?

894
47:31.079 --> 47:33.581
The kind of woman Mr. Yoon likes…

895
47:36.334 --> 47:39.170
[door opens, closes]

896
47:42.465 --> 47:43.549
What did he want?

897
47:44.008 --> 47:45.968
Did he pull rank on you? Keep you in check?

898
47:46.427 --> 47:47.804
Uh… yeah.

899
47:48.346 --> 47:49.514
Where are you going, sir?

900
47:49.597 --> 47:51.974
I don't think I need to report everything to you, do I?

901
47:52.475 --> 47:53.393
Go ahead and go home.

902
47:55.353 --> 47:56.354
By the way,

903
47:56.437 --> 47:57.939
are you the one who moved it?

904
48:01.275 --> 48:03.027
I mean Jerry's bowl in the garden.

905
48:04.987 --> 48:06.989
Oh, do you mean the silver bowl out there?

906
48:07.532 --> 48:08.574
I didn't touch it, sir.

907
48:08.658 --> 48:09.575
Really?

908
48:14.831 --> 48:16.749
[tense music playing]

909
48:18.042 --> 48:20.378
[door opens, closes]

910
48:22.255 --> 48:24.465
[suspenseful music playing]

911
48:46.946 --> 48:47.947
Stop there. That one.

912
48:48.364 --> 48:49.449
[keyboard key clicks]

913
48:49.741 --> 48:50.908
The man in the cap.

914
48:50.992 --> 48:52.910
See if you can track his movements.

915
48:52.994 --> 48:54.412
[keyboard keys clacking]

916
49:02.587 --> 49:04.422
-Hold on a sec. -[keyboard key clicks]

917
49:07.216 --> 49:09.051
"3108."

918
49:10.052 --> 49:13.139
[suspenseful music continues]

919
49:13.222 --> 49:14.807
[phone buzzing]

920
49:20.354 --> 49:21.272
How'd it go?

921
49:22.064 --> 49:23.357
[Captain Park] "3108"?

922
49:23.441 --> 49:24.525
Wait a minute.

923
49:26.444 --> 49:27.445
"3108."

924
49:30.907 --> 49:32.450
[Captain Park] Huh? Where is he going?

925
49:32.533 --> 49:33.743
Hey, try to catch up. Change lanes.

926
49:33.826 --> 49:35.411
-Follow closer. -[horn honking]

927
49:35.495 --> 49:37.079
-[tires screeching] -[both grunt]

928
49:41.042 --> 49:42.460
You sure it's 3108?

929
49:52.094 --> 49:53.513
If that's the case, then…

930
49:54.055 --> 49:55.431
there's more to this than we thought.

931
49:55.515 --> 49:58.684
Do you think it's possible that someone else is after him too?

932
49:58.768 --> 50:01.020
On the day of the accident, Park Min-hwan…

933
50:01.103 --> 50:03.314
may have carried something downstairs, right?

934
50:03.397 --> 50:05.107
If that's what they're after,

935
50:06.192 --> 50:07.568
does that change things at all?

936
50:08.277 --> 50:11.864
Captain, are you sure this is just an unnatural death case?

937
50:13.157 --> 50:15.743
[tuts] That's enough. Get back here.

938
50:16.786 --> 50:17.703
[phone beeps]

939
50:19.997 --> 50:20.915
[sighs]

940
50:20.998 --> 50:24.168
[Captain Park] Someone else out there is hunting for Park Min-hwan.

941
50:37.014 --> 50:38.850
[low tense music playing]

942
50:43.437 --> 50:46.065
[low suspenseful music playing]

943
50:52.113 --> 50:53.906
[comical music sting]

944
50:54.657 --> 50:56.409
[rattling effect]

945
51:03.541 --> 51:04.458
[squeaking effect]

946
51:04.542 --> 51:05.459
[gulps]

947
51:06.168 --> 51:07.086
[squeaking effect]

948
51:11.674 --> 51:12.925
[breathes nervously]

949
51:13.718 --> 51:16.137
[low suspenseful music continues]

950
51:19.181 --> 51:20.808
[hurried footsteps]

951
51:32.612 --> 51:33.529
[gulps]

952
51:38.367 --> 51:39.285
[relieved sigh]

953
51:54.050 --> 51:57.178
[Jae-hee] Yoon Yi-jun, you're going down.

954
52:06.103 --> 52:07.021
[lock clicks]

955
52:13.069 --> 52:14.195
[breathes nervously]

956
52:18.282 --> 52:19.200
[switch clicks]

957
52:30.920 --> 52:31.837
[Jae-hee groans]

958
52:33.047 --> 52:35.466
I don't think the phone would be in here though.

959
52:41.180 --> 52:43.349
[Jae-hee] All I see is artwork on the wall.

960
52:50.231 --> 52:51.190
Hmm?

961
52:52.900 --> 52:54.068
Hold on a minute.

962
52:58.656 --> 52:59.782
This one's crooked.

963
53:00.408 --> 53:04.245
[Yi-jun] This is a one-liter bottle. I drank 250 mL, right?

964
53:04.745 --> 53:05.955
What should that leave me with?

965
53:06.747 --> 53:07.623
[Yi-jun] Then you noticed it?

966
53:08.791 --> 53:10.001
Well?

967
53:10.668 --> 53:13.671
[Jae-hee] The lights seem dimmer than they were before I left yesterday.

968
53:14.338 --> 53:17.341
So… I'm not the only one to notice it?

969
53:17.425 --> 53:18.426
[sighs]

970
53:19.135 --> 53:22.138
He acted like such a stickler for fine details, and yet…

971
53:26.350 --> 53:27.977
-[rattling] -[gasps]

972
53:28.060 --> 53:30.479
[intriguing music playing]

973
53:31.939 --> 53:34.608
[gasps] What?

974
53:43.576 --> 53:44.577
[clacks]

975
53:49.582 --> 53:50.666
Why don't we start…

976
53:50.750 --> 53:53.878
with the reason the chairman's office summoned you before me?

977
53:53.961 --> 53:57.089
Ah, nothing gets past you, does it, problem child?

978
53:57.173 --> 53:58.883
Hey, let's talk when we get there.

979
53:59.633 --> 54:00.968
Where's your wad of gum today?

980
54:01.469 --> 54:03.721
-Wad of gum, my foot. -Hmm.

981
54:03.804 --> 54:06.515
I mean, you two seem to have grown quite close already.

982
54:06.599 --> 54:08.434
I heard you paid for his cab fare…

983
54:08.517 --> 54:10.102
and let him sleep over.

984
54:11.270 --> 54:12.271
[sighs]

985
54:12.354 --> 54:15.941
I should have known when I let Mr. Gu return to work.

986
54:16.025 --> 54:17.109
[Si-hyun] It's Mr. Jung.

987
54:17.193 --> 54:19.862
Not Mr. Gu, not Mr. An, but Mr. Jung.

988
54:20.404 --> 54:23.074
So spill it. Why'd you call your wad of gum last night?

989
54:23.157 --> 54:24.909
He's not my wad of gum, okay?

990
54:24.992 --> 54:25.910
[scoffs]

991
54:26.827 --> 54:28.120
[Yi-jun] Are you the one who moved it?

992
54:28.996 --> 54:30.539
I mean Jerry's bowl in the garden.

993
54:30.623 --> 54:32.958
Oh, do you mean the silver bowl out there?

994
54:33.042 --> 54:35.795
-Hold on. -[suspenseful music playing]

995
54:35.878 --> 54:38.297
I never told him that it was made out of silver.

996
54:38.839 --> 54:40.758
-Wh-What? -[gasps]

997
54:41.592 --> 54:43.803
-Turn the car around. -Uh, why?

998
54:43.886 --> 54:45.387
[raises voice] Turn the car around now!

999
54:45.471 --> 54:48.474
[tires screeching]

1000
54:54.355 --> 54:56.816
[drawer rattling]

1001
55:11.872 --> 55:13.290
[exclaims]

1002
55:13.999 --> 55:15.000
This is it!

1003
55:18.129 --> 55:19.964
Looks like our next farewell chat…

1004
55:21.090 --> 55:23.425
will be in the interrogation room, Mr. Yoon.

1005
55:25.928 --> 55:28.347
[door creaking]

1006
55:33.853 --> 55:35.104
-[dramatic music sting] -[startled gasp]

1007
55:38.399 --> 55:40.985
[tense music playing]

1008
55:45.072 --> 55:46.407
Too bad…

1009
55:46.490 --> 55:49.952
there isn't some reporter hack to take the blame for you in my house.

1010
55:53.455 --> 55:56.542
I'm really looking forward to hearing you wriggle out of this.

1011
55:57.418 --> 55:58.919
Come on, what's your excuse?

1012
56:00.171 --> 56:01.172
[inhales sharply]

1013
56:05.467 --> 56:07.469
Why do you keep sneaking around my home?

1014
56:07.970 --> 56:11.473
What's so interesting about the places I explicitly told you not to go in?

1015
56:11.557 --> 56:13.309
-[Jae-hee gasps] -[sighs]

1016
56:15.269 --> 56:16.103
Get out.

1017
56:20.149 --> 56:21.609
You… are fired.

1018
56:21.692 --> 56:24.028
Just get out. Get out of my house right now!

1019
56:24.111 --> 56:25.112
[Jae-hee panting]

1020
56:28.199 --> 56:30.492
I did it 'cause what you said to me at the columbarium

1021
56:30.576 --> 56:31.994
has been bothering me, sir.

1022
56:32.745 --> 56:34.872
There must have been a reason you didn't want me in there,

1023
56:35.539 --> 56:37.291
so I wanted to find out what it was.

1024
56:37.374 --> 56:39.710
Weren't you just buttering me up to gain my trust

1025
56:39.793 --> 56:41.629
so you could keep the paychecks coming?

1026
56:44.089 --> 56:48.010
Then you shouldn't care whether I killed someone or am killing someone

1027
56:48.552 --> 56:50.471
or plan on killing someone.

1028
56:54.183 --> 56:55.476
I can't look at you.

1029
56:55.976 --> 56:56.977
Get lost.

1030
56:58.646 --> 56:59.647
No.

1031
57:01.315 --> 57:02.900
[Yi-jun breathes deeply]

1032
57:02.983 --> 57:06.362
Whether you're a suspect or not actually matters now.

1033
57:10.491 --> 57:11.659
Oh, it matters now?

1034
57:12.660 --> 57:13.744
Ah, then come on, tell me.

1035
57:13.827 --> 57:16.121
How much is it gonna take for me to buy your silence?

1036
57:16.205 --> 57:17.957
-That's not what I-- -Then what do you want?

1037
57:18.040 --> 57:20.626
There's something wrong in this house and I don't know what it is.

1038
57:21.335 --> 57:23.754
-That milk… -[rattling]

1039
57:27.216 --> 57:28.133
Oh!

1040
57:29.551 --> 57:30.386
[grunts]

1041
57:32.846 --> 57:33.681
[gasps]

1042
57:35.516 --> 57:38.352
[dramatic operatic music playing]

1043
57:47.444 --> 57:51.699
[inaudible]

1044
57:56.745 --> 57:57.663
[exhales]

1045
58:10.509 --> 58:12.845
[Da-woon] Well, as for Mr. Yoon's type of girl…

1046
58:12.928 --> 58:15.180
-[Yi-jun pants] -To be honest,

1047
58:15.764 --> 58:18.017
I've only seen Mr. Yoon get drunk once,

1048
58:18.434 --> 58:20.602
and it was on the day of his mother's memorial service.

1049
58:20.686 --> 58:22.688
They should be someone brave.

1050
58:25.774 --> 58:27.318
Someone that's…

1051
58:28.485 --> 58:30.029
totally fearless

1052
58:31.447 --> 58:32.531
and gutsy.

1053
58:34.199 --> 58:35.367
Someone like that.

1054
58:35.909 --> 58:37.244
Hey, you call that ideal?

1055
58:37.745 --> 58:40.414
A beautiful woman is usually at the top of the list, right?

1056
58:40.497 --> 58:41.582
[Yi-jun groans]

1057
58:42.041 --> 58:43.417
Someone pretty doesn't…

1058
58:44.752 --> 58:46.170
have what it takes.

1059
58:46.253 --> 58:47.338
To do what?

1060
58:47.838 --> 58:51.175
Beautiful people don't have the strength…

1061
58:53.093 --> 58:55.763
to support me in this wretched…

1062
58:57.014 --> 58:58.849
Taekang empire.

1063
58:59.516 --> 59:00.726
That's why…

1064
59:01.393 --> 59:04.813
I'm still here waiting and waiting.

1065
59:06.774 --> 59:08.609
-Waiting for what? -[scoffs]

1066
59:11.028 --> 59:13.238
A brave knight on a white steed.

1067
59:15.574 --> 59:18.827
[Yi-jun] A totally fearless, gutsy knight

1068
59:19.620 --> 59:22.206
-on a white steed. -[hoofbeats effect]

1069
59:22.289 --> 59:24.333
[horse neighing effect]

1070
59:24.416 --> 59:27.127
[music swells]

1071
59:27.211 --> 59:28.087
[glass shattering]

1072
59:28.337 --> 59:30.506
LOVE IN DISGUISE

1073
59:31.215 --> 59:34.134
[closing theme music playing]

1074
59:56.824 --> 59:58.158
SPECIAL THANKS TO KIM DO-YOON, JUNG YOO-MIN, AND PARK JUN-MUYN

1075
59:58.242 --> 01:00:00.285
[Jae-hee] Strange things are happening.

1076
01:00:00.369 --> 01:00:01.995
[Yi-jun] Just pretend you don't know anything.

1077
01:00:02.079 --> 01:00:03.831
If we keep this up, you'll end up resenting me.

1078
01:00:03.914 --> 01:00:05.416
What do you want? Name your price.

1079
01:00:05.499 --> 01:00:07.334
[Na-jung] Where is Mr. Park Min-hwan right now?

1080
01:00:07.418 --> 01:00:09.753
[Hye-jung] The chairman will probably name his successor.

1081
01:00:09.837 --> 01:00:11.213
[Tae-sik] I want results.

1082
01:00:11.296 --> 01:00:14.591
My successor shall be announced at the next meeting.

1083
01:00:14.675 --> 01:00:16.844
[Yi-jun] You're being really kind and considerate.

1084
01:00:16.927 --> 01:00:18.011
It's weird.

1085
01:00:18.095 --> 01:00:19.638
-Come with me. -I will not!

1086
01:00:20.305 --> 01:00:21.223
[yells] Hey!

1087
01:00:21.306 --> 01:00:23.934
[Jae-hee] That thing that you know but I don't… what is it?

1088
01:00:24.017 --> 01:00:25.853
You didn't do it, did you, sir?
